ering\nFinance and Risk Engineering\nMathematics\nMechanical and Aerospace Engineering\nTechnology, Culture and Society\nTechnology Management and Innovation\nDegrees & Programs\nBachelor of Science\nMaster of Science\nDoctor of Philosophy\nDigital Learning\nCertificate Programs\nNYU Tandon Bridge\nK12 STEM\nResources\nUndergraduate\nGraduate\nRecords & Registration\nDigital Learning Services\nTeaching Innovation\nImpact Areas\nSustainability\nQuantum\nEmbodied Intelligence\nEngineering Health\nSystems Engineering\nEngineering & Culture\nResearch\nOffice of Research\nCenters & Institutes\nLabs & Groups\nStudent Research\nLife at Tandon\nStudent Life\nCareer Hub\nEntrepreneurship\nExperiential Learning\nMakerSpace\nSupport & Resources\nEngage\nAlumni\nGiving\nIndustry Engagement\nAbout\nOverview\nMission\nFast Facts\nHistory\nLeadership\nResearch Magazine\nCommunity\nOur Engineers\nBrooklyn\nVisit\nNews & Events\nNews\nEvents\nSocial Media\nACADEMICS | PROGRAMS\nComputer Science, Ph.D.\nComputer Science and Engineering\nDoctor of Philosophy\nOn Campus\nWith the growing prevalence of AI, the field of computer science is rapidly changing, and doctoral education in computer science must evolve to meet the moment. In response to these demands, NYU is thrilled to announce a newly-merged Ph.D. in Computer Science through a collaboration between the NYU Tandon School of Engineering and the Courant Institute. The unified Ph.D., offered through the Courant Institute beginning in Fall 2026, combines the exceptional strengths of Courant and Tandon on foundational math, computing principles, and hand-on engineering applications, offering a breadth of expertise and a range of research opportunities that are truly unique.\nAdmission to the program is highly competitive. We seek creative, articulate students with undergraduate and master's degrees from top universities worldwide.\nFor more information, visit the Computer Science Ph.D. website.\nPh.D. Admission\nExplore additional N